sections.content:
Use this hook to read the active language from a custom component inside a LanguageProvider:

```tsx
import { useDesignSystemLanguage } from '@traxion-global/design-system/react';

function MyComponent() {
  const language = useDesignSystemLanguage(); // 'es' | 'en'
  return <span>{language === 'es' ? 'Hola' : 'Hello'}</span>;
}
```

Without a LanguageProvider ancestor, the hook returns `'es'` (the context default).
